From: ininjagod98 <181880040+ininjagod98@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 10:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Minemora - do not block the event loop while disconnecting

Connection#disconnect waits on the channel close future with
awaitUninterruptibly(). Seven call sites reach it through
PacketSendListener#thenRun after sending a disconnect packet
(ServerLoginPacketListenerImpl, ServerCommonPacketListenerImpl,
ServerConnectionListener, RateKickingConnection and three inside Connection
itself). On the io_uring transport the write completion is delivered from the
completion queue, so those listeners run on the event loop thread and Netty's
checkDeadLock() throws BlockingOperationException.

Two consequences: a full stack trace per kick, and - because the throw happens
on the line before it - disconnectionDetails was never assigned, so the reason
was lost and every kick logged as the generic "Disconnected".

Blocking on the event loop was never valid, which is exactly what Netty is
reporting, so the wait is skipped there and kept for callers off the loop. The
close itself is already in flight in both cases. The details are now recorded
before the close so the reason survives regardless of which path runs.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/network/Connection.java b/net/minecraft/network/Connection.java
index 46bd47d370eee854bb7dcbe40be5488dfc6ef02f..7ced4ce0f9fda5d2b490888ea036892eab0fbf34 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/network/Connection.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/network/Connection.java
@@ -712,8 +712,24 @@ public class Connection extends SimpleChannelInboundHandler<Packet<?>> {
         }
 
         if (this.isConnected()) {
-            this.channel.close().awaitUninterruptibly();
+            // Minemora start - do not block the event loop while closing
+            // Recorded before the close, not after: the await below used to throw
+            // BlockingOperationException on the io_uring transport and this assignment
+            // was never reached, so the disconnect reason was lost and every kick was
+            // logged as the generic "Disconnected".
             this.disconnectionDetails = details;
+
+            final io.netty.channel.ChannelFuture minemora$closeFuture = this.channel.close();
+            // Blocking here was only ever valid off the event loop. Every
+            // "send disconnect packet, then close" path in the server registers this
+            // through PacketSendListener#thenRun, and on io_uring the write completion
+            // is delivered from the completion queue, so the listener runs on the event
+            // loop itself and Netty's checkDeadLock() rejects the wait. The close is
+            // already in flight either way; only the wait is skipped.
+            if (!this.channel.eventLoop().inEventLoop()) {
+                minemora$closeFuture.awaitUninterruptibly();
+            }
+            // Minemora end - do not block the event loop while closing
         }
     }
 
